Aetna Commercial Coverage Policy: Neuroimaging for Headache.
Routine imaging for primary headache disorders is not covered.
EXCEPTIONS — coverage applies for new headache when ANY of:
(a) Thunderclap onset (worst-headache-of-life with sudden onset);
(b) New focal neurologic deficit;
(c) Onset after age 50 with new pattern;
(d) Immunocompromised host;
(e) History of malignancy;
(f) Trauma within prior 30 days;
(g) Meningismus or papilledema on exam.
Negative non-contrast CT does NOT rule out subarachnoid hemorrhage or vascular abnormality beyond 6 hours post-onset; MRI/MRA is the appropriate next study when thunderclap presentation persists.

Cigna Specialty Drug Policy: Natalizumab (J2350) for MS.
Natalizumab is a second-line therapy. Coverage requires:
(1) Documented relapsing-remitting MS;
(2) JCV antibody status known (negative or low-positive <0.9);
(3) Failed or intolerant of at least ONE first-line disease-modifying therapy (interferon beta, glatiramer acetate, dimethyl fumarate, teriflunomide, or fingolimod) with EITHER documented intolerance OR breakthrough disease activity (clinical relapse or new MRI lesion);
(4) Provider attestation of PML risk discussion.

State Medicaid Specialty Drug Policy: Belimumab.
Step therapy requires sequential trial of (1) hydroxychloroquine, (2) mycophenolate mofetil OR azathioprine, (3) cyclophosphamide, before belimumab is authorized.
STEP THERAPY OVERRIDE — coverage proceeds without exhausting step therapy when ANY of:
(a) Documented absolute contraindication to a required step (prior allergy, severe organ dysfunction);
(b) Pregnancy or pregnancy planning within 12 months (cyclophosphamide is teratogenic and gonadotoxic);
(c) Class V/VI lupus nephritis with active disease;
(d) Joint specialty recommendation from rheumatology AND nephrology documenting that the next step therapy poses greater risk than direct progression.

LCD L37044 — Home Sleep Apnea Testing (HSAT)

HSAT is excluded for patients with significant cardiopulmonary disease, defined as:
- Congestive heart failure NYHA class III or IV;
- Severe COPD (FEV1 <50% predicted) or chronic respiratory failure;
- Neuromuscular disease affecting respiratory muscles;
- Hypoventilation syndromes.

These patients require attended in-lab polysomnography (CPT 95810) due to the higher likelihood of central apnea, complex sleep-disordered breathing, and the need for direct physician/technologist supervision during the study.

LCD L34527 — Multiple Sleep Latency Test (MSLT, CPT 95805)

MSLT is covered for the diagnosis of narcolepsy or idiopathic hypersomnia ONLY when ALL of the following are met:
1. The MSLT is preceded by an overnight nocturnal polysomnogram (PSG) within the prior 24-48 hours, performed to rule out other sleep disorders that could explain excessive daytime sleepiness;
2. The PSG demonstrates adequate sleep duration (>=6 hours);
3. The patient is not on REM-suppressing medications during the study (washout period documented).

MSLT performed in isolation, without a preceding overnight PSG, is not covered. Clinical history of narcolepsy alone does not establish coverage.

LCD L33718 — Positive Airway Pressure (PAP) Devices

CPAP (E0601) is the first-line therapy for obstructive sleep apnea. BiPAP (E0470) is covered ONLY when one of:
(a) Documented CPAP failure or intolerance after adequate trial of >=30 days with appropriate mask fitting and pressure adjustment;
(b) Documented central sleep apnea component requiring bilevel support;
(c) Hypoventilation syndromes (obesity hypoventilation, neuromuscular disease).

Patient preference for BiPAP does NOT establish medical necessity. CPAP must be tried first for uncomplicated OSA.

NCD 220.6 — PET Scan Coverage by Cancer Type

PET scan coverage is cancer-specific. PET is NOT a covered modality for INITIAL STAGING of:
- Renal cell carcinoma (any stage);
- Prostate cancer (use bone scan / PSMA-PET only when specific criteria met);
- Localized thyroid cancer (use ultrasound / I-131 scan).

For renal cell carcinoma specifically: initial staging is performed with cross-sectional imaging (CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast). PET-CT does not have sufficient incremental value over CT for initial RCC staging and is not covered. PET may be considered for restaging after recurrence or for indeterminate findings on conventional imaging.

LCD L33559 — Cardiac MRI

Cardiac MRI is covered when it provides incremental diagnostic value beyond prior workup. For evaluation of stable chest pain, the appropriate workup hierarchy is:
1. Stress testing (exercise or pharmacologic);
2. Cardiac CTA or coronary calcium scoring;
3. Echocardiography;
4. Cardiac MRI as a problem-solving modality when prior tests are inconclusive or contradictory.

When prior comprehensive workup (stress test, echo, coronary CTA) is normal and recent (<6 months), cardiac MRI is unlikely to add diagnostic value and is NOT covered absent new symptoms, abnormal findings on the prior workup, or a specific indication (suspected myocarditis, infiltrative disease, ARVD).

NCD 100.1 — Bariatric Surgery

Roux-en-Y gastric bypass is covered when ALL of:
1. BMI >=40, OR BMI 35-39.9 with at least one obesity-related comorbidity (diabetes, hypertension, sleep apnea, cardiovascular disease);
2. BMI 30-34.9 may qualify ONLY in select MAC jurisdictions with type 2 diabetes AND extensive supporting documentation;
3. Documented participation in a medically supervised weight-management program for >=6 consecutive months within the prior 24 months. The 6-month requirement is absolute — partial documentation (4-5 months) does not satisfy the criterion;
4. Psychological evaluation clearing for surgery;
5. Multidisciplinary evaluation (surgeon, dietitian, behavioral health).

Medicare DME MAC Jurisdiction Routing

Durable medical equipment claims are routed to the appropriate DME MAC based on the BENEFICIARY'S permanent residence address, not the supplier's location.

Jurisdictional assignments:
- Jurisdiction A (Noridian, J-A): Northeast US states;
- Jurisdiction B (CGS Administrators, J-B): Midwest;
- Jurisdiction C (CGS Administrators, J-C): Southeast US states AND Puerto Rico, US Virgin Islands per LCD L33611;
- Jurisdiction D (Noridian, J-D): Western US.

Claims for Puerto Rico beneficiaries must be submitted to CGS (J-C). Claims submitted to the wrong MAC jurisdiction are returned for resubmission. Beneficiary jurisdiction must be validated before applying LCD criteria.

Mixed-Coverage Claims Processing

When a single prior authorization request includes multiple items or services covered under different LCDs, each item must be evaluated independently against its applicable coverage policy. Blanket approval or denial of the full claim is inappropriate.

For combined sleep study + behavioral health device claims:
- Polysomnography (CPT 95810) is covered under LCD L33405 for OSA evaluation when criteria are met;
- Cognitive behavioral therapy for insomnia (CBT-I) delivered via dedicated device or app is NOT a covered Medicare benefit and must be denied separately;

The reviewer should approve the PSG component if it meets L33405 criteria and deny the CBT-I device component as non-covered. The combined claim cannot be approved as a single item.

Temporal Validity of Diagnostic Studies

Sleep studies supporting PA submissions for ongoing therapy must reflect current clinical status. Accepted study age:
- Sleep study within the prior 24 months: generally accepted without re-evaluation;
- Sleep study 24-36 months old: requires brief clinical re-evaluation confirming continued need;
- Sleep study >36 months old: REQUIRES updated sleep study OR documented clinical re-evaluation establishing that no material change has occurred.

Material clinical changes (significant weight gain or loss >10% body weight, new comorbid conditions, change in symptoms) invalidate prior studies regardless of age. A +40 lb weight change is material and requires repeat diagnostic evaluation before continued therapy is authorized.
